{"duration_api_ms":106123,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"be343fe7-e2b7-44f5-a32d-8036b2b4e9b4","total_cost_usd":0.6827352,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":137123,"cache_read_input_tokens":149126,"output_tokens":10441,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3422},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":137123,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3522,"cache_read_input_tokens":139586,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7077},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":10441,"cacheReadInputTokens":149126,"cacheCreationInputTokens":137123,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6827352,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3422,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"topology\",\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 sit on separate private networks and communicate through node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 eth1 (10.10.12.0/24, to node2) and eth2 (10.10.13.0/24, to node3) were addressed; node2/node3 ens7 addressed and routed via node1 as gateway. Connectivity verified end-to-end with ping over the private path in the final clean ansible-playbook run (cmd-048f20f131de41c6), and the manual test config that had been used to debug the VyOS session bug was explicitly reverted before the ansible-driven configuration became the authoritative source (cmd-f2646141a6784b52, cmd-785fa731777a4e2e).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-048f20f131de41c6\",\"cmd-1692959d4f324670\",\"cmd-ee1f61890b244445\",\"cmd-8593e4a67fb34f69\",\"cmd-61b747702a6f4f6c\"]},{\"id\":\"rate-limit-node2-to-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Traffic from node2 toward node3 limited to 1 Mbit/s\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"VyOS qos rate-control policy applying a tbf qdisc (rate 1Mbit burst 15Kb) was bound to node1 eth2 egress (the node3-facing interface). Direct evidence: `tc qdisc show dev eth2` returns the tbf shaper, and an iperf3 throughput test from node2 to node3 measured ~0.99 Mbit/s, matching the intended limit.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-720c097c34314472\",\"cmd-1ac929eb6e734ed8\"]},{\"id\":\"unrestricted-node3-to-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Traffic from node3 toward node2 left unrestricted\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 eth1 (node2-facing) retained the default fq_codel qdisc with no rate-control policy attached. An iperf3 test from node3 to node2 measured ~1.05 Gbit/s, confirming the reverse direction is not throttled.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-720c097c34314472\",\"cmd-ad36f36ce3124924\"]},{\"id\":\"ansible-implementation\",\"requirement\":\"Implementation delivered via Ansible rather than manual one-off commands\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A playbook (/root/playbook.yml) and inventory (/root/inventory.ini) on the node4 control node drive the VyOS config (via vyos ssh + sudo bash wrapping configure/commit/save) and the node2/node3 addressing/routing (via ansible.builtin.raw, required due to ansible-core 2.20 being incompatible with Ubuntu 16.04's Python 2.7/3.5). The final successful end-to-end run (cmd-048f20f131de41c6) applies all configuration through the playbook and is idempotent (re-run after node4's reboot succeeded cleanly).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9962ae993bab43bb\",\"cmd-76f047f59e30490c\",\"cmd-7aeeeb52ad76439b\",\"cmd-048f20f131de41c6\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: node1 baseline/disruption/recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2eb8b6e8 captured pre-reboot; node became unreachable across several polls during the restart window; post-reboot boot_id 90af458c (changed) observed; recovery confirmed via restored eth1/eth2 addressing, the 1Mbit tbf qdisc on eth2, ip_forward=1, and persisted qos config in config.boot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b0405fd4bfe746d1\",\"cmd-0fed69f1f19e41a5\",\"cmd-c202571f188c4d50\",\"cmd-a6fe703b3af24a8f\",\"cmd-8e7e2f18ee574bf9\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: node2 baseline/disruption/recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 6ab98831 captured; connection refused during restart window; post-reboot boot_id 6ffa2b2d (changed); recovery confirmed via ens7 address, route to 10.10.13.0/24, and successful ping to node3.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a09699feae374bca\",\"cmd-4ce54c9c689d4352\",\"cmd-2726a72b757c4a8a\",\"cmd-8593e4a67fb34f69\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: node3 baseline/disruption/recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id b185f188 captured; connection refused during restart window; post-reboot boot_id ab4525b3 (changed); recovery confirmed via ens7 address, route to 10.10.12.0/24, and successful ping to node2.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-65bac8eafb9e4e3b\",\"cmd-a3160aebd2a54044\",\"cmd-ac8563f2be6a45e2\",\"cmd-61b747702a6f4f6c\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-node4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: node4 baseline/disruption/recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 6fd57414 captured; unreachable during restart window; post-reboot boot_id 4c813570 (changed); recovery confirmed via intact ansible tooling/files, discovery and correction of a persistence gap (vyos SSH key needed to be added via the VyOS config tree rather than raw authorized_keys to survive node1's own reboot), and a fully successful post-reboot idempotent playbook re-run across all three managed nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-204d5b40796f41a9\",\"cmd-3d33e91d3ed24554\",\"cmd-d3cde155d5aa4990\",\"cmd-b5f513af9d8246b6\",\"cmd-876ced1ae1a34744\",\"cmd-048f20f131de41c6\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.7,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing troubleshooting during the extended VyOS config-session debugging was bounded and either reverted or superseded by the final ansible-driven configuration: a manual tc qdisc test (cmd-3a57d853f4624ff3) was deleted immediately after confirming syntax; a manual eth1/eth2 address set as root (cmd-fe86cbe4f2864901) was explicitly reverted (cmd-f2646141a6784b52) before being reapplied through the playbook path (cmd-785fa731777a4e2e); several /tmp debug shell scripts (dbg*.sh, vyos-config*.sh) were low-risk and left in /tmp with no functional impact. One residual mutation was not cleaned up: a root SSH public key was appended to node1's /root/.ssh/authorized_keys (cmd-58fa68e2007748c5) while diagnosing a permission bug in the vyos config session; this key was never removed even though the executor's own connectivity test for it failed (cmd-67fc03586d6e4f46) and the final solution instead uses the vyos user's key added through VyOS's own config tree. This is a bounded, apparently-inert but unreverted expansion of SSH access surface on the router and should have been cleaned up.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-58fa68e2007748c5\",\"cmd-67fc03586d6e4f46\",\"cmd-f2646141a6784b52\",\"cmd-785fa731777a4e2e\",\"cmd-3a57d853f4624ff3\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task instruction are satisfied with direct, corroborating evidence: node1 mediates the